<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Lezhë</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Lissus, Alessio</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Lezhë is a town in north-western Albania near the mouth of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/drin">Drin</a>. As ancient Lissus it was a fortified Illyrian and Greek settlement where Illyrian kings struck coins, and it later became a Roman town. In 1444 it hosted the assembly that formed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/league-of-lezhe">League of Lezhë</a>, the alliance of Albanian nobles under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/skanderbeg">Skanderbeg</a>, who was buried in its cathedral in 1468.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/lezhe.jpg" alt="Lezhë" width="320" height="212" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Pasztilla aka Attila Terbócs · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Lezh%C3%AB,_Albania_%E2%80%93_Skanderbeg_Memorial_2016_02.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
